    {"t": "p", "text": "Support size (the number of features shared by the SRS sample and the candidate analog, k in the tables) modulates every distance. Distances computed on k=3 features are geometrically shallower than distances on k=19: fewer shared features give the pair more chances to agree by omission. The tables therefore report k alongside every distance, and Section 5 makes the reading rule explicit: an analog at moderate distance with large k beats a closer analog on small k. This is also why the same sample can carry different analog distances in different panels: each panel is a different slice of chemistry with its own support."},

