    {"t": "p", "text": "All 51 SRS closure-residual vectors were projected through the same pipeline. In the sludge panel, all 51 land in a single cluster (C3) at the 95th percentile or beyond of that cluster's member distances; in the radionuclide panel they split across three clusters (C4: 33, C6: 16, C0: 2) but again all 51 land at or beyond the 95th percentile; in the salt panel none can be projected, because the closure basis reports none of the salt anion suite. Read together: the conservative residual source terms are compositionally unlike anything in the Hanford current-inventory library, the model assigns them to the rim of whatever cluster is least unlike them, and the salt comparison is impossible on that basis. This is the quantitative version of the first white paper's central basis warning, obtained without ever labeling a single row by site or basis."},
